Z||000009||Jncomutt||08-22-2001||03:46 PM||||Will he bore out the TB for my 4Cyl too???||||reg||1
Z||000010||Nashco||08-22-2001||05:08 PM||||I overheard Darrel talking to a 2.5 owner with a turbo, asking if he could bore the 2.5 T.B.  Darrel said if you supplied a core so that he could investigate it and try the machining.  Throttle bodies are all pretty similar, the only thing that limits the amount it can be bored is the vacuumm lines cast into the part.  Most throttle bodies have a few millimeters clearance cast into them, so you can bore more or less depending on the factory tolerances.<P>Give Darrell a call and he'll talk to you about it and help you out; he's a really good guy and easy to talk to.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||DreXteR||08-22-2001||08:44 PM||||Wich is the diameter of the stock 2.8 throttle body?<P><BR>Thanx<P>DreX||||reg||5
Z||000012||DreXteR||08-23-2001||04:57 PM||||Top||||reg||1
Z||000013||MinnGreenGT||08-23-2001||05:07 PM||||My car is running both Darrel's Bored-out TB and Intake Plenum.  Added them shortly after finishing the High-Output 3.1L.  Yes, it does make some difference (every little change helps!) engine just breaths better (also running ported stock exhaust manifold, high-flow cat, no mufflers, and port & polished heads). And the engine still looks stock (except non-engraved intake on an '87).<P>I think (note the word: THINK) that the Fiero is stock @ 52mm or 53mm and Darrel takes them out to 57mm or 58mm (increase of 5mm either way).  I believe it is rated to increase flow area by 13%.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/strut1.jpg">  note: the Strut-Tower brace is also from Darrel (traded for my old intake plenum-'cause I won the other at a Fiero Christmas Party  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000014||Dave Gunsul||08-23-2001||05:42 PM||||I too am using Darrels bored out t-body and upper plenum and am very satisfied! Very noticable gain too. The stock t-body is 52mm.<BR>I was so impressed with his work that I had him port my lower intake as well and have bought his new rasied roof plenum that i'm going to put on next year, as i'm hand polishing it right now.<P><BR>I'd also like to second what was said about<BR>Darrel. He is a great guy and a credit to the Fiero community!<BR>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver<p>[This message has been edited by Dave Gunsul (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000015||johnt671||08-23-2001||06:24 PM||||I e-mailed Darrel last month about my 2.5 t.b.  He said he can only bore it out 5/32 )if I remember correct) and was unsure of any gains from it.  I still may do it as the only other choice seems to be a $350.00 unit from The Fiero Store that is probibly overkill for my near stock 2.5||||reg||1
Z||000016||c m west||08-23-2001||07:44 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WCF_Intake_(FA51).jpg"> <P> this unit is for sale here at West Coast Fiero - it is a 3.4 Twin Dual Cam throttle body addapted to a 2.8 intake plenum<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>||||reg||1
